# Runtime logs generated by services/tests
logs/
.isolation-report.json
.pytest-run.log

# Per-service ed25519 identity material. The private halves are the
# whole mechanism: a key seen by two services makes them one principal,
# and the 26-of-32 defect this was built to close comes straight back.
# The key MAP holds only public halves and is safe to read, but it is
# generated per deployment and mounted read-only, so it does not belong
# in git either — a committed map is one a pull request can edit.
secrets/service-identity/

# Item-8 transient outputs. These names are EXPERIMENT-SHAPED: a tracked
# item8-results.jsonl is indistinguishable from real evidence by name,
# and D291 committed one containing six calibration rows bound to a real
# tree SHA before the experiment had ever run. `git status` called the
# tree clean precisely BECAUSE the artefact had been committed. (D292)
item8-results.jsonl
item8-toolchain.txt
item8-run.log
item8-derived/
item8-identity/
